<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Île-de-France</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Île-de-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> is the region around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in northern France and the historic heart of the French monarchy. Under the early Capetian kings the royal domain consisted chiefly of this area and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a>, from which royal power gradually expanded over the kingdom. Today it is France's most populous region, with Paris as its capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ile-de-france.jpg" alt="Île-de-France" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David McSpadden from Daly City, United States · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eiffel_Tower_from_the_Tour_Montparnasse_3,_Paris_May_2014.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
